{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/usr/bin/python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path\nPath('\\\\''/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-s7/collab/1791377000000-architect-s7-signoff.gpt-6-astra.findings.md'\\\\'').write_text(\\\"Created-GMT: 2026-10-07 12:57:00 GMT\\\\nCoding-Agent: codex\\\\nRole: Lead System Architect\\\\nTask: architect-python-c3-s7-signoff\\\\n\\\\n# Python C3 Slice S7 — Architectural Sign-Off\\\\n\\\\n**Lead System Architect Sign-Off: WITHHELD.**\\\\n\\\\nThe runtime architecture is sound on inspection, and the corrected CPython rulings are implemented consistently. Landing approval is withheld because the required integration/mutation evidence is incomplete and one post-S6 Python composition was not migrated. These are concrete completion requirements; no architectural redesign is requested.\\\\n\\\\n## Review basis and scope\\\\n\\\\nReviewed the working tree on branch yang-python-c3-s7; HEAD and origin/master both resolve to 49960017efef87195920061dd3436063e97a4812. S7 is uncommitted, with its new corpus and gate files untracked; those files were read explicitly because git diff origin/master does not include them.\\\\n\\\\nAuthorities: docs/design/datom.world.md; docs/design/yang.antlr.md section 8.5; collab/1791270000000-architect-python-c3-s6-s7-design.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md; collab/1791275000000-orchestrator-s7-gate-rulings.md; docs/agents/build-n-test.md. Reviewed the production diff, changed test compositions, PM1/PM2 tests, conversion/repetition tests, data-module tests, corpus generator and gate/parser binding, fixture changes, golden changes, early review, engineer report, orchestrator record, and target/profile/changed-{clj,cljs,cljd}.log.\\\\n\\\\nThis is an independent source/evidence review, not a new execution of the three Clojure lanes. The supplied green fast-lane results and clean formatting are accepted. I independently executed both Python generators under /usr/bin/python3 -I -B (CPython 3.9.6), intercepting only Path.write_text in memory to compare generated bytes without rewriting fixtures.\\\\n\\\\n## Blocking findings\\\\n\\\\n### S7-1 — Required integration gate is not demonstrated (high)\\\\n\\\\nThe green changed-only results are real, but they do not establish the S7 integration gate:\\\\n\\\\n- target/profile/changed-cljs.log:21 explicitly says SKIP slow test c3-gate-test; line 36 skips sequence-repetition-boundary-test.\\\\n- target/profile/changed-cljd.log:165 explicitly skips c3-gate-test; line 404 skips sequence-repetition-boundary-test.\\\\n- The JVM changed-only task excludes slow tests by contract; c3-sources-on-every-vm-test and c3-gate-test are marked :slow.\\\\n- Other conversion, numeric-key, heap and prelude semantic bodies are also skipped in the recorded cross-host fast runs.\\\\n\\\\nDesign section 2.6 and docs/orchestrator-log.md:10557 require changed Python slow tests on JVM, Node/Dart slow lanes, and one bb test:all run with counts recorded. The latest orchestrator record at lines 10600–10609 records only test:changed. The engineer report remains IN PROGRESS and lists focused tests, mutations, goldens and Node/Dart slow sides as next work. No supplied ruling withdraws the slow/full gate.\\\\n\\\\nRequired closure: execute or supply traceable successful final-tree logs for the prescribed slow/full gate, including the ten corpus programs on four VMs on all three hosts and JVM naive/hooked source execution. Record counts and the reviewed revision/tree. Do not interpret registered test counts that include guarded SKIPs as executed corpus coverage.\\\\n\\\\n### S7-2 — Ruling-14 mutation evidence is missing (high)\\\\n\\\\nThe design requires actual red-then-reverted evidence for disabled promotion, skipped demotion, double-coerced keys, omitted floor adjustment, tag-3 abs(n), and narrowed shift counts, plus the cited S6 scalar-gate evidence. The supplied S7 engineer report contains no mutation results and explicitly leaves mutations pending.\\\\n\\\\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md now says the mutation evidence is in that report and marks S7 landed. Those completion claims are not supported by the current artifact. The DeepSeek findings file contains only an unrecognized-model error; it is not an additional completed review.\\\\n\\\\nRequired closure: finish the mutation ledger, identifying each mutation, detecting test/host, observed failure, and restoration; reference the actual S6 scalar evidence. Re-run relevant checks after restoration. Update the report and completion wording to match demonstrated state. Existing test definitions are useful detectors but are not evidence that the prescribed mutations were caught.\\\\n\\\\n### S7-3 — S6 heap-test composition bypasses the new profile contract (medium)\\\\n\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/int_heap_test.cljc:29–38 still registers data through its one-argument registrar and never calls prelude/admit. It constructs and runs Python prelude guest programs, so it is a Python composition, not an exempt generic data-module test.\\\\n\\\\nDesign section 3 explicitly requires migrating this composition after rebasing S7 onto S6. The current registry lacks data/max-items and would be refused by the newly required admission check. Existing heap cases can remain green because they need not invoke repetition; that does not establish a valid admitted Python profile.\\\\n\\\\nRequired closure: register data with {::data/max-items 1048576}, then call prelude/admit after the integer registrar. Include the S6 heap namespace in final slow verification. This also makes the documentation'\\\\''s “Every Python composition calls it” statement true for the in-tree test compositions inspected.\\\\n\\\\n## Architectural and implementation findings that pass inspection\\\\n\\\\n- **Layering and invariants:** Only prelude.cljc and data.cljc change production behavior. Limits remain explicit immutable composition values; no hidden global state, mutable configuration, callback, new effect channel, AST schema, Jing encoding, heap/store protocol or UCF profile field is introduced. Python-specific refusal translation stays in the interpreted prelude; generic data registration remains language-independent.\\\\n- **Sequence bound:** The quotient comparison preserves the signed 64-bit Py_ssize_t interval before handling empty or negative repeats. Non-integers raise TypeError; out-of-range counts raise OverflowError. Empty sequences and negative in-range counts reduce to zero. Exact integer/mul computes the result size, integer/compare checks data/max-items, and py/int-result translates either a bit-limit breach or an item-limit breach to MemoryError with empty args before the repetition loop. py/imul computes the repeated value before cell/set\"'!, preserving a list on refusal. Scope remains repetition, as ruled; incremental growth is not silently assigned this limit.'\"\\\\n- **Data module:** The one-argument registrar retains its existing exports. The two-argument registrar validates a positive native integer through exact-integer?, exclusion of big carriers, and pos?, then adds an arity-checked, pure, zero-argument export. No default is smuggled into the registry. Tests cover absence, explicit registration, invalid input, arity and four-VM access.\\\\n- **Admission:** prelude/admit checks every declared host name using the registry'\\\\''s dotted resolution path, deterministically sorts all missing names, emits the specified qualified refusal data, and returns the original registry on success. This implements name admission, not full callable/profile attestation, consistent with the bounded interim design and later linker requirement discovery.\\\\n- **Profile portability:** PM1 names the three missing version-4 integer exports and missing data/max-items. PM2 lifts a version-1 2\"'^100 result, resumes under the small registry, checks that limits are absent from the body, and ties the resumed value to the S0 small-profile outcomes. No execution-profile identity is added to content.'\"\\\\n- **round and keywords:** The float branch checks ndigits type before the deliberately unsupported round(float, ndigits) result. Non-numeric x retains the missing-__round__ TypeError first. pow/round retain keyword acceptance per the governing measured ruling; adding :no-kw would be incorrect. int(x=...) remains the documented divergence.\\\\n- **Corpus design:** Ten named programs distinguish eight CPython measurements from two labelled profile hand pins. Source/docstring/parser-packet binding prevents independently drifting portable packets. Tests compare exact stdout and absence of an exception, with all four VM runners; JVM source tests also exercise no-op hooks. The generator now rejects blank output lines.\\\\n- **Goldens:** The five affected prelude/image addresses are updated and the hook-prelude address is unchanged. Recorded fast-lane verification supports the checks actually executed; skipped image/semantic bodies still require S7-1 closure.\\\\n- **Ledger:** The new overflow and round-order measurements, lint-scope docstring, deferred Unicode repr work, accepted shift allocation class and NaN-sign limitation are consistent with the supplied rulings.\\\\n\\\\nNo additional production-code correctness defect was established in this review. That observation does not substitute for the missing acceptance runs.\\\\n\\\\n## Verification evidence\\\\n\\\\nExisting fast-lane logs confirm:\\\\n\\\\n| Lane | Tests | Assertions | Result |\\\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\\\\n| JVM | 254 | 7,831 | 0 failures, 0 errors |\\\\n| Node CLJS | 227 | 3,124 | 0 failures, 0 errors; slow bodies skipped |\\\\n| ClojureDart | 207 | not reported here | All tests passed; slow bodies skipped |\\\\n\\\\nIndependent CPython 3.9.6 regeneration compared byte-identically:\\\\n\\\\n- int-conv-v1.txt: 1021 measured rows; SHA-256 5164c8fe632c113ffdfae72be347d6b7b3c8e2fbb744804c01a08b63ac065db4.\\\\n- c3-corpus-v1.txt: 10 programs; SHA-256 1b430c4c6d5fea0edc2fd6147b954d405fdeb8935ba476c97ecda5f367c76914.\\\\n\\\\nThe CPython run verifies the keyword and round-order oracle without relying on the withdrawn early interpretation. Hand-labelled limit outputs remain profile pins, not CPython measurements.\\\\n\\\\n## Landing decision\\\\n\\\\n**WITHHELD for S7-1, S7-2 and S7-3.** Close the missed composition, supply the required final-tree slow/full and mutation evidence, and reconcile completion claims before requesting landing sign-off again. The production design is suitable to proceed through that gate; the current evidence is insufficient to declare C3 S7 complete.\\\\n\\\\nOnly this findings artifact was written by the reviewer; source, tests and fixtures were not changed.\\\\n\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
